  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Statistics II: standard deviation using an assumed mean</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 3.1: Use an assumed mean to find the mean and standard deviation from a frequency table.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question C7 in Section C of Chapter 2 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P. and Shilton, S., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Statistics 1 for Edexcel, Cambridge University Press, 2004: set as a frequency table with a given assumed mean, with new Kenyan contexts and new data.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
