    <node><name>2</name><description>Subtracted mean of d</description><answertest>NumAbsolute</answertest><sans>ans3</sans><tans>mnsign</tans><testoptions>0.0501</testoptions><quiet>0</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt3-3-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>You subtracted the mean of \(d\) from \(A\). The mean is \(A + \dfrac{\Sigma fd}{\Sigma f}\).</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>-1</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt3-3-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>A mean of \({@ans3@}\) would need \(\Sigma fd = {@n@} \times ({@ans3@} - {@A@}) = {@need@}\). Compare that with your \(\Sigma fd\) in (a).</p>]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
